156	/* A CLOSE OR DETAIL SHOT HAS NO WINDOW, only its light. A blind grade on October 9th found a fly
157	 * standing as tall as a window pane and a mullion running through a glass vial: a lens that close is
158	 * focused on the subject, and the room behind it is out of focus colour. So nearer framings lay the
159	 * region as a soft wash, with no frame to cross anything. The second grade found the first wash (blur
